nning big and changing your  life forever people get carried away by  their passion and make rash decisions so  it's something to be cautious of but at  the same time without passion you can't  even fall in love  he explains it's all a balancing act and  some people just can't keep their  balance but to hikari life is gambling a  series of making decisions and taking  risks to achieve your dream and anyone  who says that they hate gambling  just doesn't understand things correctly  they love gambling too what they hate is  loss that sometimes comes with it and  this whole monologue comes to a peak  with him saying that he loves passion  and that passion is gambling and  gambling is life and that love is  control it's a pretty interesting  perspective to take and although we've  only seen a little bit of akari so far  i'm kinda digging him i feel like he's  going to be a very self-serving  character and that might open the doors  to him siding with whoever might benefit  him the most in that situation and that  could have some very chaotic  implications in this way he sort of  reminds me of hisoka from hunter hunter  understanding how the world works and  using that to put yourself in the most  advantageous position maybe and  hopefully the parallel isn't exactly  one-for-one  [Music]  but the methodical chaos vibe is  definitely still here rather than  hisoka's drive for powerful opponents  though hikari wants to control the  country's passion with his fight club if  he can just make people love his fight  club he will gain control of them  just think about all the people you know  who are die hard sports fans or fans of  games for example they are passionate  and part of their world revolves around  that property  in a way that industry behind it  controls part of their lives  and as such they have some control over  the risks and actions that people are  willing to take it's a very interesting  philosophy that i want to see expanded  on more hakari feels that now is the  time to put his plan into action the  public has learned about her spirits to  some extent so there's surely going to  be interest in the idea of these  sorcerers who fight those spirits  fighting each other and jiu jitsu  headquarters is slowly crumbling so  there really isn't anyone who can get in  the way of these plans but he can't make  these moves alone so he asks itadori to  become his pawn and get swept away by  his passion itadori remembers back to  megami telling him to be discreet about  jujitsu high and as they've been talking  about gambling this whole time he begins  asking for a croupier wanting a second  opinion on what's going on however they  get cut off as hikari's phone starts  rigging and a clear suspicion crosses  his face and here we get a situation  which both shows off how clever hikari  is and how naive itadori is hikari  offers him a drink and asked if he knew  that gojo can't handle his liquor and  itadori who is still only thinking of  distancing himself from jiu jitsu high  in hikari's eyes asks who's gojo  pretending to not know him at first  glance this might seem like the best  thing he could have said however then  you remember that gojo is effectively a  rock star in the jujutsu world every  sorcerer alive knows who he is so  pretending not to know him was probably  the most suspicious thing that itadori  could have done leading to hikari  immediately knowing that he is from  jujutsu high and going on the offensive  and here we get the first glimpse of his  curse technique as sliding doors appear  at itadori's sides and slam closed  trying to smash into itadori it seems  that just like toto's clapping hikari  actually has to slide his hands together  to make these doors closed which is kind  of neat it also kind of reminds me of  the kuchi sakayona which is the spirit  that ghetto was using that had scissors  which worked in similar ways although  this seems to be a bit less effective  version of that in that one is doors and  the other is giant scissors he  eventually manages to pin itadore's neck  and arm between the doors in what is  effectively a pillory before kicking him  across the face and explaining that a  call from kirara was a clear sign for  emergency itadore breaks free for a  moment and bashes his head into hikaris  before calling out for him to listen as  hakari says that he just doesn't want to  just as that battle reaches its climax  we hop over to megami and panda on the  roof with kirara megami is pleading with  kirara and explaining that right now  they aren't from jujutsu high they're  just people who are trying to solve a  massive act of jiu jitsu terrorism and  to do that they need hikari's help  however kirara doesn't seem too  interested as apparently the higher-ups  are the ones who chose to leave him and  hikari out in the first place so if they  didn't want their help then they don't  need it now panda explains that the  higher-ups are very conservative both in  stance on regulation and in how jujutsu  is to be used he says that nobara's  curse technique is the perfect example  of what they like to see while things  like hearst videos or hakaria's  techniques are example of what they hate  to see i would kind of like a bit more  clarification on what this means i  understand like the cursed video thing  but i'm not sure the intrinsic  difference between nobara's technique  and khakari's technique so maybe a  little bit of a better definition would  have been great here also a quick side  note which might just be a translation  issue or could also be a sign of hope or  i could just be reading too much into  things we've been given some vague hints  leading to the idea of nobara being dead  i believe last time they brought it up  it was met by solemn sadness rather than  ah she's recovering she'll be fine or  even she's recovering but we'll see how  it goes but here panda says kugisaki's  curse technique is a model jujutsu that  conservatives would like is not was like  they would say for a dead person like i  said it might just be my english teacher  brain going into overdrive but this  section might also be a hint that nobara  is returning words matter but we'll see  how much it's also interesting that they  chose her specifically when so many  characters exist that there has to be  another good example out there so why  would you choose a dead girl heck even  with megami being a zenin i'm assuming  his own abilities would be a better  example plus it would just be good use  of literary technique to bring her up  shortly before we learn the truth either  way kirara is not having it clearly  angry at how hikari was treated in the  past and sure that no matter what  happens gojo will just clean up their  mess anyways  so why even bother coming to them for  help just that in itself is suspicious  but that's when megami drops the bomb  that gojo was sealed and that's why they  lost in the first place we get this  panel where kirara looks both shocked  and on the verge of bursting out  laughing at the idea that gojo could  have been defeated and clearly he still  doesn't believe them realizing that  talking is going to get them nowhere  megami decides to change things up as he  uses rabbit escape to summon a horde  no a murder of bunnies much better  however it doesn't look like he's gonna  be using them offensively at all he  looks kind of embarrassed almost like  he's pouting a little bit saying that he  needs to persuade kirara so negotiations  with hakari can go further now this  could go in two ways firstly he could  just be trying to win over kira with  some cute animals this would 100 work on  me but i don't think it's likely what's  going on here second and much more  likely he might be trying to overwhelm  kirara's curse technique if how the  ability works has to do with people who  have been marked or if there's a limit  on how many things can be repelled with  this effect then sending dozens and  dozens of bunnies at him might be a good  solution either way i am curious to see  what happens next as this is where the  chapter comes to a close while not a lot  happened in the grand scheme of the  story this chapter we did get a few  things that i really appreciate and that  really stood out to me is very important  firstly the monologue from hikari gave  us a glimpse at who he really was or at  least his philosophies and how he sees  the world around him which i really  liked we also got to see his ability to  think quickly as he gets itadore to  expose himself and not to mention we  also got to see our first look at his  curse technique which was pretty simple  but very cool we got what might be a  hint of nobara still being alive and of  course we had kirara being confronted  with the reality that gojo is sealed  even if he doesn't believe it things  have been progressing towards the climax  and i think next chapter should be the  moment where everything comes to a head  and god am i excited is it next week yet  nope let me know what you guys think of  this chapter as well as hikari's curse  technique the idea of nobara still being  alive and most importantly what do you  think megami will do with his murder of  bunnies if you enjoyed this jujutsu  kaizen video and want to see more please  leave a like and if you're new to anime  uproar remember to subscribe and ring  that bell by selecting all notifications  you can guarantee that you will not miss  any future videos and of course you can  always follow anime uproar at anime  uproar on twitter or instagram or you  can follow myself at excellionyt i want  to give a big thank you to all of our  anime uproar patrons who make videos  like this one possible special thanks to  alpha sigma who is an absolute mad lad  and disciple of lord tuigo himself and  of course are the one tier patrons the  ones who rise above all other clans  these being ingrata patahepha al-jatal  hinokami and water the toasted chi the  spike  8227 dylan